{
  "type": "mod",
  "id": 2738,
  "hub_id": null,
  "guid": "com.dandy.gflvoices",
  "name": "GFLVoices",
  "slug": "gflvoices",
  "teaser": "Just cover your manly face up",
  "thumbnail": "https://forge-static.sp-tarkov.com/mods/E61PzvNODNOW5DaGmILeISL4G6p4ny5mCDJgilFh.png",
  "downloads": 704,
  "favourites_count": 3,
  "description": "<h1>Preview</h1>\n<div class=\"youtube-lite\" data-video-id=\"SePHCUUOKSM\" data-embed-url=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/SePHCUUOKSM?autoplay=1\"><img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/SePHCUUOKSM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"YouTube video thumbnail\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" /></div>\n<h1>GFLVoices</h1>\n<p>Adds the dolls’ voices from GFL2 to Tarkov</p>\n<p>Recommend you use SchizoPMC because since there isnt a lot of voice files to work with, I just decided to use the triggers from that mod.</p>\n<p>Im considering having bots use them but Im not sure how to do it without splitting this into 50+ different mods per voice lmao</p>\n<h2>Voice List</h2>\n<p>So far everyone currently released in gfl2 except for Soppo(Im sad), Mityl, Faelynn and Welrod</p>\n<h2>Installing</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Download the mod.</li>\n<li>Extract the archive using 7-Zip or WinRAR.</li>\n<li>Place the extracted folder into your main SPT directory.</li>\n<li>Launch the game.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Uninstalling</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Change your selected voice back to a default voice.</li>\n<li>Delete the <code>GFLVoices</code> folder from your SPT installation.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Issues</h2>\n<p>If there are any, just put it in the comments. Ill try my best to fix it.</p>\n<p>P.S. Idk why but I had to restart my game for some voice changes to take effect, if u somehow still have the voice of a previous character after switching, just restart ur game.</p>\n",
  "detail_url": "https://forge.sp-tarkov.com/mod/2738/gflvoices",
